{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1563138-homebrewing-simple-merits-and-backgrounds","id":1563138,"title":"Homebrewing Simple Merits and Backgrounds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-08-16T03:07:26-07:00","id":1563138,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Homebrewing Simple Merits and Backgrounds","content":"The idea here is to extrapolate from existing official material to expand options for particular use cases, discussing balance and tips on how to avoid traps in the process.<br /> <br /> It's also to discuss the quality of official material as it informs the direction new stuff can take and how far they should get.<br /> <br /> My initial questions/proposals are for V5 as it is what I'm currently playing, but this thread should work just fine for all lines and editions, including to propose adaptations from one to the other. <hr /><br /> So, to the point. My current character is a game designer and also cooks as a hobby that's getting some momentum. Both are also means to exert influence over mortals. V5 has four Haven modifiers that circle around the effects I want, but don't quite hit it:<br /> <br /> Library and Laboratory are each ranked 1+ and give you their value as a bonus for a particular Specialty while in your Haven. Each has a list of skills, but you have to define a single Specialty for the benefit. Each dot has the same cost as a normal Specialty and they're Corebook options.<br /> <br /> I can get something like Technology (Coding) with Laboratory (despite not fitting the fluf of it), but a broader bonus for making games specifically is not an option, nor is Craft (Cooking) available.<br /> <br /> The Player's Guide presents Machine Shop, and it works very similarly except it is way broader in actual use: if your Haven is 2+ you don't chose a Specialty, instead it applies to every roll to physically deal with equipment in general, not limited to Crafts, and ostensibly adds an incinerator if you have Machine Shop 3 and a car compactor if your Haven is also 3.<br /> <br /> Anyone with experience running V5 can say if Machine Shop is ok as basis or too strong? I want to adapt it for both games and cooking, so I can get the bonus in things like writing the game's story and whatnot, and have something for Cooking that also help with other crafts or something, maybe chemistry, idk. I also make things like my own cookie molds in there.<br /> <br /> For reference, the corebook also has Location, another Haven modifier that has more broad possible applications, can only be bought at 1 dot, but gives a +2 bonus to related rolls. <hr /><br /> On another, but related note, how could those Backgrounds be adapted to Legacy? I think the overall idea is too sound to not be ported, but I'm unsure if the current rules for Library are the best approach.<br /> <br /> And if anyone found an interesting way to use the Vehicle background in the V6 Playtest, I'd like to know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T10:27:37-07:00","id":1563180,"title":"","content":"I unfortunately can't help with the V5/V6 questions, but I ran into similar problems with the Library Background before. At the time I looked up all instances I could find and got this list:<br /> <br /> <b>Library</b><br /> <br /> Variant 1:<br /> Roll Mental Attribute + Library Rating to uncover general information<br /> <br /> Variant 2:<br /> Roll Library Rating vs Difficulty 7 (or 8) to save 1 XP per success while raising an Ability or Advantage<br /> <br /> Variant 3:<br /> \u25cf\u25cb\u25cb\u25cb\u25cb +1 die on (Topic) rolls<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cb\u25cb\u25cb +1 die on (Topic) rolls, -1 on (Topic) difficulty<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cb\u25cb +2 dice on (Topic) rolls, -1 on (Topic) difficulty<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cb +2 dice on (Topic) rolls, -2 on (Topic) difficulty<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf +3 dice on (Topic) rolls, -2 on (Topic) difficulty<br /> <br /> Variant 4:<br /> 1 auto-success per dot on (Topic) rolls<br /> <br /> Variant 5:<br /> -1 Difficulty per dot on 'research' rolls<br /> <br /> The problem seems to be that the different variants assume different types of libraries (either general or specialized) and their function (research, learning, reference).<br /> My solution at the time was to split the Background into Library (general) and Library (topical) that behave differently.<br /> <br /> A general Library covers a variety of topics and the question becomes whether it covers the particular topic to research. It usually can not cover topics in the same depth a dedicated Library can.<br /> Variant 1 matches that the best, with a few modifications:<br /> Roll Mental Attribute + Library Rating against a Difficulty that matches the obscurity of the topic. If you want to apply the research, add a number of dice equal to the successes to the application roll.<br /> TBH, these types of Libraries can be mostly replaced with a general research roll in modern settings by just looking things up on the internet.<br /> <br /> Specialized Libraries should award a higher benefit for learning, reference, and specific research. The simplest way to me was to add +1 dice per dot for applications. I think the XP bonus use is fair on these, too, if you use it for study.<br /> You can have that Background multiple times to see how deep they cover different topics, so Library (Cooking) and Library (Game Dev) as separate Backgrounds.<br /> <br /> That idea could be applied to 'Dedicated Space With Tools', ie a Laboratory, Workshop, or Studio. I would say that a general Workshop functions differently to a specialized one - you could probably cook a meal in your garage by jury-rigging some tools, but it's a different thing to do it in a well equipped kitchen.<br /> <br /> So a general Workshop could use the 'Attribute + Rating vs Task Difficulty provides extra dice' formula, while specialized Workshops lower the Difficulty -1 per dot for their task. Similarly, you could have a Workshop (Smithy) to create cooking utensils, a Workshop (Kitchen) to cook, and a Workshop (Game Dev). I also see no reason why you shouldn't be able to practice skills and talents in them for the XP save on advancements.<br /> <br /> With that, specialized Libraries would increase the dice pool (= better theoretic basis) and Workshops lower the Difficulty (= right tools make it easier).<br /> <br /> That only leaves the question how to handle situations when you want to use your specialized Workshop or Library for tasks outside of their scope, but I would leave that to common sense. You can use a Game Dev rig to brute force a password, or look up some general programming in your Game Dev library. The ST can always adjust the bonus accordingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-18T03:58:47-07:00","id":1563219,"title":"","content":"My problem with Variation 1 is that it interacts badly with Knowledge Abilities. You either use your knowledge or your library. It also doesn't cover well a search on libraries in general as something you can do. I think it's better handled as a revision in Knowledges to make them more &quot;you know stuff and where to get the correct info&quot; than just &quot;you remember facts. Or not&quot;. My own experience as trained scientist is that the most important part of learning a field isn't to collect facts, but the techniques and methods to judge and understand sources.<br /> <br /> Variant 2 I personally despise. I never liked the idea of saving XP through dice rolls or buying traits to save on buying other traits.<br /> <br /> Overall I think general use libraries, workshops and the like are basically equipment. They are not special backgrounds, just you having the basic tools for a task. To qualify as a background it must have something special about it, including but not necessarily limited to being specialized in a topic.<br /> <br /> The Machine Shop modifier plays on that aspect to a degree. It doesn't cover &quot;Craft: Machines&quot;. Instead it covers &quot;any roll where you physically explore a machine with tools&quot; by having an advanced equipment set rather than a regular one, including having a huge variety of tools beyond what would be regularly expected, going fully &quot;in doubt, you have it no matter how peculiar it is&quot;, as it includes things like a repair shop that also has a 3D printer at the ready.<br /> <br /> Overall I think extra dice work well. I understand the appeal of variant 3 to avoid unyielding pools, but I'd rather leave Diff out of the picture for Backgrounds. The question is, bonus dice when? Which rolls should benefit vs just being allowed? Is a per Specialty take the best approach at all?<br /> <br /> As an improvised ruling I'd be personally wary of applying bonuses outside the focus of the trait. If it works for something, that's basic &quot;you can roll&quot; and that's it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}